      "writtenOn": "2022-01-13T23:52:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you verify my logic here? There are effectively three cases where timer overflow could have occurred after disabling interrupts and reaching here:\n\n1) before \"t0 \u003d get_time()\"\n2) between \"t0 \u003d get_time()\" and \"next_delay \u003d ...\"\n3) after \"next_delay \u003d ...\" and before this check\n\nCase (1), the timestamp \"t0\" could be referring to previous \"epoch\" since clksrc_high was not updated.\n\nCase (2), __hw_clock_event_get() refers to previous \"epoch\" since the *match interrupt* (not overflow interrupt) should have triggered an update to its value.\n\nCase (3) we don\u0027t care about, but no way to avoid.",
